module

public import Sheaf.RingTheory.KoszulDualComplex
public import Sheaf.RingTheory.KoszulRegularSequence
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Homology.DerivedCategory.Ext.Linear
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Ext.HasExt

/-! # Ext computed by a finite free Koszul resolution

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0BQZ, local finite free Koszul computation.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace ExteriorAlgebra

/-- A Koszul resolution computes Ext by the cohomology of its signed dual.
Source: Stacks Project, Tag 0BQZ, the equality of derived Hom with the total Hom
of the finite free Koszul resolution (blueprint: lem-sc-koszul-ext-dual-homology).

Proof: Give the Koszul complex its standard quotient augmentation. In degree
zero the image of the first differential is the ideal generated by f, so the
augmentation induces the quotient isomorphism. In positive degrees its homology
vanishes by hreg. Each term is projective: it has the finite exterior basis of
the standard basis of A^r. Thus this augmented complex is a projective resolution
of A/I. Apply the projective-resolution Ext/cohomology comparison to Hom(-,A).
The integer total Hom complex with target A[0] has exactly one possibly nonzero
component in each nonnegative degree n, namely Hom(K_n,A), and zero negative
components. Its differential is signed precomposition with d_(n+1), with sign
(-1)^(n+1), which is the definition of koszulDualBoundary. Evaluating at the
unique component identifies its cycles and coboundaries with those of the
signed dual complex. The induced quotient isomorphism is A-linear, since all
component maps and both Ext and cohomology scalar actions are A-linear.
Take its degree-r linear equivalence. No determinant or conormal module is used;
this comparison holds in degree zero and for a zero quotient as well. -/
theorem exists_koszul_ext_dual_homology_equiv
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [HasDerivedCategory.{u + 1} (ModuleCat.{u} A)]
    (I : Ideal A) (r : ℕ) (f : Fin r → A)
    (hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsKoszulRegular f) (hf : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = I) :
    Nonempty (Abelian.Ext (ModuleCat.of A (A ⧸ I)) (ModuleCat.of A A) r ≃ₗ[A]
      (koszulDualComplex A r f).homology r) := by sorry

end ExteriorAlgebra
